From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:24:08 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: add the chiptop syscon to xrx500.dtsi

The xRX500 keeps a page of chip-level configuration registers one
0x80000 step above the RCU, at physical 0x16080000. Nothing in this
tree describes it yet, and nothing needs to bind a driver to it: it is
a grab bag of single fields that belong to other blocks' bring-up
sequences, reached by phandle from whoever owns the block.

The PCIe support landing next needs two of them. The root complexes
drive an endianness word at +0x4c, one inbound and one outbound
byte-swap bit per port; the serdes PHYs drive the IFMUX reference-clock
gate at +0x120, one enable bit per PHY. Both go through
syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle() on an "intel,syscon" property, so the
node has to exist and has to carry "syscon" in its compatible list
before either driver can probe.

Describe it as a plain syscon, alongside cgu@16200000 which is already
one. The address is the vendor tree's chiptop@00080000 (AVM 4.9
arch/mips/boot/dts/lantiq/xrx500.dtsi) resolved out of its
ssx4@16000000 wrapper, whose ranges are <0x0 0x16000000 0x02000000>,
into the flat absolute form this dtsi uses throughout. The size is the
vendor's as well.

No "simple-mfd": unlike the RCU this node has no children, and the
registers it holds have no owner of their own.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
index 8426bfbed168..319eb8de4b11 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
@@ -54,6 +54,15 @@ cgu: cgu@16200000 {
 		#clock-cells = <1>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Chip-top configuration block: a pure syscon. Consumers reach single
+	 * fields through a phandle plus an offset.
+	 */
+	chiptop: syscon@16080000 {
+		compatible = "intel,grx500-chiptop", "syscon";
+		reg = <0x16080000 0x1000>;
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * Reset Control Unit. The mainline lantiq,xrx200-reset driver must be
 	 * a syscon child: its reg is a byte offset into the parent regmap,
